YASD Cav-Hum-Mal-Law

I am currently in the process of the trying to achieve my third
ascension, this time lawful human Caveman. Caveman is similar to my
previous Barbarian in that it is strong from the beginning and are
poor spellcasters. But unlike Barbarian, Caveman starts with very weak
weapons, making the early game so much harder.

After several false starts I got a character going, that looked like
it can make it to ascension. I won't bore you with details, only recap
the main points:

- amulet of reflection from Sokoban
- found bones of Adrake the Wizard in Gnomish Mines containing cloak
of magical resistance
- got magic marker from shop in Minetown
- bought a long sword and dipped for Excalibur (which turned to be of
-1 enchantment)
- got a wish from throne (speed boots)
- got a wish from fountain dipping in Minetown (bag of holding)
- from the Castle wand I got two wishes (scrolls of charging and ring
of levitation)
- found marker in Chromatic Dragon's cave (which I lost somehow)
- got another wish from fountain dipping, this time in dlvl 1 when I
was mass diluting potions (magic marker)
- after the quest I still had no scroll of enchant armor (really, I
had identified all the scrolls I had); I had to blind-write the
scroll, which took four tries to succeed

Anyway, when I plunged into Gehennom i was AC -33 with HP 126 wielding
+7 Excalibur. Asmodeus' lair was the first level of Gehennom, so I
levelported to VS level with him and proceeded up using him to find
upstairs. All looked fine until I reached Orcus. The environment got
rather dense, but still manageable and I proceeded to dig my way
towards upstairs. Sometime along the way, Dispater was summoned. This
did not distress me at all, I have killed Dispater before without any
trouble. But this time it was different, he chewed through my hit
points with alarming speed. I was burdened, so I teleported him away,
dropped my BoH, took out potions of extra healing I tried to recover,
but he was back in next turn; and when another attempt to buy more
time by teleporting him away failed, it was all finished for me. One
more turn and I am dead. He was able, literally, to kill me in three
rounds.

What I did wrong:
- forgot to use Elbereth -- when will I ever remember
- was burdened even with dropped BoH
- too low max HP; at this stage of game HP 126 is not enough, even
with high AC


